<title>UK: Wassall to float General Cable stake - paper.</title>
<headline>Wassall to float General Cable stake - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Industrial group Wassall Plc is to float off 70 percent of its wholly-owned General Cable unit, clearing the way for Wassall to raise its stake in TLG Plc, the Daily Telegraph said on Monday.</p>
<p>The paper said the stake in General Cable, unrelated to the quoted British cable company of the same name, would be sold in the United States, Canada and on the international markets.</p>
<p>Wassall last month bought a four percent stake in TLG, the lighting group spun off by then Thorn EMI in 1995. This sparked talk of a possible bid, the paper said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
